{
  "key": "framework",
  "typeName": "Framework Agreement",
  "source": "Derived 20 October 2026 from the approved framework agreement pack (5 Packs to check/03 framework agreement, cut from the firm's November 2025 framework agreement, the owner's chosen base) by reading its headings with skeletonCheck.js. Its deal-specific articles (an earlier option agreement, a project company, a lease transfer, surrender and first refusal) are decisions or optional; the investment agency agreement read beside it is a different form (appointment, duties, resignation) and is not merged. Presence: an article (level 1) is \"always\" when every firm precedent of the family read for the study has it, \"optional\" when it belongs to one deal or one form, and \"decision\" when a drafting decision (decisions/framework.json) turns it on or off. Sections (level 2) are the pack's own, all optional except the ones every precedent has; they are listed so that a section the firm already uses is never reported as a new clause.",
  "completeLevels": [
    1,
    2
  ],
